th scattered singles (3, 7, 8, K, A). Attempting a straight (3-4-5-6-7-8) would disrupt the 444 triplet and 55/66 pairs, leaving weak singles (5, 6) and a less cohesive hand. The pair straight (44-55-66) also results in a surplus of singles. The most effective strategy is to utilize the triplet structure.\n\nReason: Playing the lowest triplet (444) with the lowest single (3) as a kicker is the most efficient way to clear low-value cards. This move preserves the pairs (55, 66, 99) and high triplets (QQQ, 222), maintaining a balanced hand with strong control cards (three 2s, one K, one A) to handle opponent responses.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦3", "♠4", "♥4", "♦4"]}'}
